{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## LIVE VALIDATION against the deployed MCP server — AC1, AC2, AC4 MET; AC3 NOT MET\n\nAll calls made through https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp against container\n`rebar-mcp-2dbdcc8abe2c-8093` (image = `2dbdcc8abe2c`, current origin/main).\n\n**AC1 — MET.** `review_plan` with DEFAULT arguments on `b928-3ab6-5985-417b` returned a real\nplan-review verdict, not a ref-resolution error: `verdict: PASS`, `llm_ran: true`,\n`llm_calls: 4`, `source: attested`, `verified_at_sha: 2dbdcc8abe2c…`, 0 blocking / 1 advisory.\nSubject chosen because it is open and unblocked, so the gate could not fast-fail before\nreaching the LLM stage.\n\n**AC2 — MET.** `verify_completion` with DEFAULT arguments on `62ab-c11e-30c2-40be` returned a\ncompletion verdict: `verdict: PASS`, 5/5 criteria `met: true` each with a file+line citation,\n`certifiable: true`, `signable: true`, `record.signed: true`, `requests: 12`,\n`tool_calls: 13`, `llm_ms: 60044`, `verified_at_sha: 2dbdcc8abe2c…`.\n\n**AC4 — MET.** Verified inside the container:\n`REBAR_ROOT=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code`, and\n`git -C /var/gerrit/site/mcp-code rev-parse origin/main` →\n`2dbdcc8abe2c110543819d059a2b3bb63c82fb13`. A real object DB reachable by the gate ops.\n\n**AC3 — NOT MET.** `plan_review_status(b928)` through the same server returns\n`verdict: foreign_key`, not `certified`. Reason given verbatim: *'this environment has no\nop-cert public key; it cannot certify any signature'*. The attestation IS produced\n(`attestation.signed: true` on the AC1 run) — it simply cannot be certified where it was\nsigned. This is the gap this ticket's own Scope-boundaries section already routes to\n`dire-expectable-terr…`, but AC3 as written demands `certified`, so it is left UNCHECKED\nrather than reworded. Escalated to the operator.\n\nNot ticking DD1, which requires AC1-AC3."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787903082144889001,"uuid":"35d04be9-ded7-4665-8521-ba6edd3aa004"}